{"id":"mahabharata-8-005","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":5,"title":"पञ्चमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 5 · Janamejaya asks and Dhritarashtra laments Karna","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks how Dhritarashtra took the news of Karna's death, and Vaishampayana tells of the king's anguish. Dhritarashtra remembers his own former honour and the strength of Karna, whom no one could face with a drawn bow.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣನ ಸಾವಿನ ಸುದ್ದಿಯನ್ನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಹೇಗೆ ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸಿದನೆಂದು ಜನಮೇಜಯ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನ ರಾಜನ ವ್ಯಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ತನ್ನ ಹಿಂದಿನ ಗೌರವವನ್ನೂ ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಹಿಡಿದ ಕರ್ಣನನ್ನು ಯಾರೂ ಎದುರಿಸಲಾಗದಿದ್ದುದನ್ನೂ ನೆನೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय पूछते हैं कि कर्ण की मृत्यु का समाचार धृतराष्ट्र ने कैसे लिया, और वैशम्पायन राजा की पीड़ा बताते हैं। धृतराष्ट्र अपने पूर्व सम्मान और कर्ण के उस बल को याद करते हैं जिसके सामने धनुष लिए कोई टिक नहीं पाता था।","te":"కర్ణుని మరణ వార్తను ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు ఎలా స్వీకరించాడని జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు; వైశంపాయనుడు రాజు వ్యథను చెబుతాడు. ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు తన గత గౌరవాన్ని, విల్లు పట్టిన కర్ణుని ఎవరూ ఎదిరించలేకపోవడాన్ని గుర్తు చేసుకుంటాడు.","ta":"கர்ணனின் மரணச் செய்தியை த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் எப்படி ஏற்றான் என்று ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்க, மன்னனின் வேதனையை வைசம்பாயனர் கூறுகிறார். த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் தன் முன்னைய மதிப்பையும், வில் ஏந்திய கர்ணனை எவரும் எதிர்க்க முடியாததையும் நினைவுகூர்கிறான்.","ml":"കർണ്ണന്റെ മരണവാർത്തയോട് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ എങ്ങനെ പ്രതികരിച്ചുവെന്ന് ജനമേജയൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; വൈശമ്പായനൻ രാജാവിന്റെ ദുഃഖം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. തന്റെ മുൻകാല മഹിമയും, ആർക്കും വലിച്ച വില്ലോടെ നേരിടാനാകാത്ത കർണ്ണന്റെ ശക്തിയും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ഓർക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.5; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"श्रुत्वा कर्णं हतं युद्धे पुत्रांश्चैवापलायिनः ।\nनरेन्द्रः किंचिदाश्वस्तो द्विजश्रेष्ठ किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king heard that Karna had been killed in battle and that his sons had not fled, and had recovered a little, best of Brahmanas, what did he say?"}},{"n":2,"text":"प्राप्तवान्परमं दुःखं पुत्रव्यसनजं महत् ।\nतस्मिन्यदुक्तवान्काले तन्ममाचक्ष्व पृच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had reached the supreme, great sorrow born of his sons' calamity. Tell me, who ask, what he said at that time."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रुत्वा कर्णस्य निधनमश्रद्धेयमिवाद्भुतम् ।\nभूतसंमोहनं भीमं मेरोः पर्यसनं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard of Karna's death, wondrous and almost unbelievable, bewildering to all beings, as terrible as the toppling of Mount Meru,"}},{"n":4,"text":"चित्तमोहमिवायुक्तं भार्गवस्य महामतेः ।\nपराजयमिवेन्द्रस्य द्विषद्भ्यो भीमकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"as unfitting as the great-minded Bhargava losing his wits, as Indra of fearful deeds being defeated by his enemies,"}},{"n":5,"text":"दिवः प्रपतनं भानोरुर्व्यामिव महाद्युतेः ।\nसंशोषणमिवाचिन्त्यं समुद्रस्याक्षयाम्भसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"as the sun of great radiance falling from the sky to the earth, as the unthinkable drying up of the ocean with its inexhaustible waters,"}},{"n":6,"text":"महीवियद्दिगीशानां सर्वनाशमिवाद्भुतम् ।\nकर्मणोरिव वैफल्यमुभयोः पुण्यपापयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"as the total destruction of earth, sky and the guardians of the quarters, as the fruitlessness of both merit and sin,"}},{"n":7,"text":"संचिन्त्य निपुणं बुद्ध्या धृतराष्ट्रो जनेश्वरः ।\nनेदमस्तीति संचिन्त्य कर्णस्य निधनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Dhritarashtra reflected carefully with his mind, thinking, \"This cannot be,\" about Karna's death."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्राणिनामेतदात्मत्वात्स्यादपीति विनाशनम् ।\nशोकाग्निना दह्यमानो धम्यमान इवाशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yet since all beings are of a nature to perish, it may be so.\" Burned by the fire of grief, his heart as if blown upon by a bellows,"}},{"n":9,"text":"विध्वस्तात्मा श्वसन्दीनो हा हेत्युक्त्वा सुदुःखितः ।\nविललाप महाराज धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"his spirit shattered, sighing, wretched and in deep pain, crying \"Alas, alas,\" Dhritarashtra, Ambika's son, great king, began to lament."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"संजयाधिरथो वीरः सिंहद्विरदविक्रमः ।\nवृषमप्रतिमस्कन्धो वृषभाक्षगतिस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sanjaya, the hero son of Adhiratha, with the valour of a lion or an elephant, with shoulders like a bull's, and a bull's eyes, gait and voice,"}},{"n":11,"text":"वृषभो वृषभस्येव यो युद्धे न निवर्तते ।\nशत्रोरपि महेन्द्रस्य वज्रसंहननो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"who like a bull never turns back in battle from another bull, a youth with a frame like the thunderbolt, matching even great Indra in battle,"}},{"n":12,"text":"यस्य ज्यातलशब्देन शरवृष्टिरवेण च ।\nरथाश्वनरमातङ्गा नावतिष्ठन्ति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"at the twang of whose bowstring and the roar of whose rain of arrows chariots, horses, men and elephants could not stand in the fight,"}},{"n":13,"text":"यमाश्रित्य महाबाहुं द्विषत्संघघ्नमच्युतम् ।\nदुर्योधनोऽकरोद्वैरं पाण्डुपुत्रैर्महाबलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"relying on whom, that strong-armed, unfailing destroyer of enemy hosts, Duryodhana made enmity with the mighty sons of Pandu,"}},{"n":14,"text":"स कथं रथिनां श्रेष्ठः कर्णः पार्थेन संयुगे ।\nनिहतः पुरुषव्याघ्रः प्रसह्यासह्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"how was that best of chariot-fighters, Karna, a tiger among men, whose valour no one could withstand by force, killed in battle by Partha?"}},{"n":15,"text":"यो नामन्यत वै नित्यमच्युतं न धनंजयम् ।\nन वृष्णीनपि तानन्यान्स्वबाहुबलमाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on the strength of his own arms, he always thought nothing of Achyuta, nor of Dhananjaya, nor of the other Vrishnis."}},{"n":16,"text":"शार्ङ्गगाण्डीवधन्वानौ सहितावपराजितौ ।\nअहं दिव्याद्रथादेकः पातयिष्यामि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'With the bow Sharnga and the bow Gandiva together, those two unconquered ones, I alone will fell them in battle from my divine chariot,'"}},{"n":17,"text":"इति यः सततं मन्दमवोचल्लोभमोहितम् ।\nदुर्योधनमपादीनं राज्यकामुकमातुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"so he constantly said to the foolish Duryodhana, deluded by greed, unwavering, anxious, craving the kingdom."}},{"n":18,"text":"यश्चाजैषीदतिबलानमित्रानपि दुर्जयान् ।\nगान्धारान्मद्रकान्मत्स्यांस्त्रिगर्तांस्तङ्गणाञ्शकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who conquered even strong, hard-to-beat enemies, the Gandharas, Madrakas, Matsyas, Trigartas, Tanganas and Shakas,"}},{"n":19,"text":"पाञ्चालांश्च विदेहांश्च कुणिन्दान्काशिकोसलान् ।\nसुह्मानङ्गांश्च पुण्ड्रांश्च निषादान्वङ्गकीचकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Panchalas, Videhas, Kunindas, Kashis, Kosalas, Suhmas, Angas, Pundras, Nishadas, Vangas and Kichakas,"}},{"n":20,"text":"वत्सान्कलिङ्गांस्तरलानश्मकानृषिकांस्तथा ।\nयो जित्वा समरे वीरश्चक्रे बलिभृतः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Vatsas, Kalingas, Taralas, Ashmakas and Rishikas, the hero who in battle defeated them and made them pay tribute in the past,"}},{"n":21,"text":"उच्चैःश्रवा वरोऽश्वानां राज्ञां वैश्रवणो वरः ।\nवरो महेन्द्रो देवानां कर्णः प्रहरतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, as Uccaihshravas is best of horses, Vaishravana best of kings, and great Indra best of gods, was the best of fighters,"}},{"n":22,"text":"यं लब्ध्वा मागधो राजा सान्त्वमानार्थगौरवैः ।\nअरौत्सीत्पार्थिवं क्षत्रमृते कौरवयादवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and having obtained him by conciliation and honour, the king of Magadha besieged the kshatriya kings, except the Kauravas and Yadavas."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा निहतं कर्णं द्वैरथे सव्यसाचिना ।\nशोकार्णवे निमग्नोऽहमप्लवः सागरे यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Karna was killed in single combat by Savyasachin, I am sunk in an ocean of sorrow like a man in the sea without a boat."}},{"n":24,"text":"ईदृशैर्यद्यहं दुःखैर्न विनश्यामि संजय ।\nवज्राद्दृढतरं मन्ये हृदयं मम दुर्भिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I do not perish from such griefs, Sanjaya, I think my heart is harder to break than the thunderbolt."}},{"n":25,"text":"ज्ञातिसंबन्धिमित्राणामिमं श्रुत्वा पराजयम् ।\nको मदन्यः पुमाँल्लोके न जह्यात्सूत जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard of this defeat of kinsmen, relatives and friends, what man in the world other than me would not give up his life, charioteer?"}},{"n":26,"text":"विषमग्निं प्रपातं वा पर्वताग्रादहं वृणे ।\nन हि शक्ष्यामि दुःखानि सोढुं कष्टानि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would choose poison, fire, or a fall from a mountain peak; I will not be able to bear these painful sorrows, Sanjaya.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"श्रिया कुलेन यशसा तपसा च श्रुतेन च ।\nत्वामद्य सन्तो मन्यन्ते ययातिमिव नाहुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For fortune, family, fame, austerity and learning, the good regard you today as they do Yayati, son of Nahusha."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्रुते महर्षिप्रतिमः कृतकृत्योऽसि पार्थिव ।\nपर्यवस्थापयात्मानं मा विषादे मनः कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In learning you are like a great sage, O king, and you have done what was to be done. Steady yourself, and do not set your mind on despair.\""}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"दैवमेव परं मन्ये धिक्पौरुषमनर्थकम् ।\nयत्र रामप्रतीकाशः कर्णोऽहन्यत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I think only fate is supreme; fie on useless human effort, since Karna, who was like Rama, was killed in battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"हत्वा युधिष्ठिरानीकं पाञ्चालानां रथव्रजान् ।\nप्रताप्य शरवर्षेण दिशः सर्वा महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having slain Yudhishthira's army and the swarms of Panchala chariots, having scorched all quarters with his rain of arrows, that great chariot-fighter,"}},{"n":31,"text":"मोहयित्वा रणे पार्थान्वज्रहस्त इवासुरान् ।\nस कथं निहतः शेते वातरुग्ण इव द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"having bewildered the Parthas in battle like the thunderbolt-handed god the asuras, how does he now lie slain like a tree broken by the wind?"}},{"n":32,"text":"शोकस्यान्तं न पश्यामि समुद्रस्येव विप्लुकाः ।\nचिन्ता मे वर्धते तीव्रा मुमूर्षा चापि जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no end to my sorrow, as one sees none to the ocean's waves. My anxiety grows fierce and the wish to die arises in me."}},{"n":33,"text":"कर्णस्य निधनं श्रुत्वा विजयं फल्गुनस्य च ।\nअश्रद्धेयमहं मन्ये वधं कर्णस्य संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of Karna's death and Phalguna's victory, I think Karna's killing unbelievable, Sanjaya."}},{"n":34,"text":"वज्रसारमयं नूनं हृदयं सुदृढं मम ।\nयच्छ्रुत्वा पुरुषव्याघ्रं हतं कर्णं न दीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"My heart must be of adamant and very hard, since it does not burst on hearing that Karna, tiger among men, has been killed."}},{"n":35,"text":"आयुर्नूनं सुदीर्घं मे विहितं दैवतैः पुरा ।\nयत्र कर्णं हतं श्रुत्वा जीवामीह सुदुःखितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods must have long ago ordained a very long life for me, since I live here in great suffering after hearing Karna was slain."}},{"n":36,"text":"धिग्जीवितमिदं मेऽद्य सुहृद्धीनस्य संजय ।\nअद्य चाहं दशामेतां गतः संजय गर्हिताम् ।\nकृपणं वर्तयिष्यामि शोच्यः सर्वस्य मन्दधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fie on this life of mine today, bereft of friends, Sanjaya. Having come to this disgraceful state, I will live a wretched life, to be pitied by all, dull-witted."}},{"n":37,"text":"अहमेव पुरा भूत्वा सर्वलोकस्य सत्कृतः ।\nपरिभूतः कथं सूत पुनः शक्ष्यामि जीवितुम् ।\nदुःखात्सुदुःखं व्यसनं प्राप्तवानस्मि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I who was once honoured by all the world, how shall I now live, charioteer, despised? I have met misfortune worse than sorrow, Sanjaya."}},{"n":38,"text":"तस्माद्भीष्मवधे चैव द्रोणस्य च महात्मनः ।\nनात्र शेषं प्रपश्यामि सूतपुत्रे हते युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the killing of Bhishma and the great-souled Drona, I see no remainder here now that the charioteer's son has been killed in battle."}},{"n":39,"text":"स हि पारं महानासीत्पुत्राणां मम संजय ।\nयुद्धे विनिहतः शूरो विसृजन्सायकान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero was the far shore for my sons, Sanjaya, and he fell in battle, hero as he was, loosing many arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"को हि मे जीवितेनार्थस्तमृते पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nरथादतिरथो नूनमपतत्सायकार्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is life to me without that bull among men? The great warrior must have fallen from his chariot, afflicted by arrows,"}},{"n":41,"text":"पर्वतस्येव शिखरं वज्रपातविदारितम् ।\nशयीत पृथिवीं नूनं शोभयन्रुधिरोक्षितः ।\nमातङ्ग इव मत्तेन मातङ्गेन निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and he must lie on the earth like a mountain peak split by a thunderbolt, adorning it, drenched in blood, like an elephant felled by a rutting elephant."}},{"n":42,"text":"यद्बलं धार्तराष्ट्राणां पाण्डवानां यतो भयम् ।\nसोऽर्जुनेन हतः कर्णः प्रतिमानं धनुष्मताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, the strength of Dhritarashtra's sons and the cause of fear to the Pandavas, the model among bowmen, was killed by Arjuna."}},{"n":43,"text":"स हि वीरो महेष्वासः पुत्राणामभयंकरः ।\nशेते विनिहतो वीरः शक्रेणेव यथा बलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero, great archer, who made my sons fearless, lies slain, like Bala slain by Shakra."}},{"n":44,"text":"पङ्गोरिवाध्वगमनं दरिद्रस्येव कामितम् ।\nदुर्योधनस्य चाकूतं तृषितस्येव पिप्लुकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a lame man's journey, a poor man's desire, a thirsty man's drops, so was Duryodhana's hope."}},{"n":45,"text":"अन्यथा चिन्तितं कार्यमन्यथा तत्तु जायते ।\nअहो नु बलवद्दैवं कालश्च दुरतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A matter planned one way turns out another way. Ah, fate is mighty and time is hard to cross."}},{"n":46,"text":"पलायमानः कृपणं दीनात्मा दीनपौरुषः ।\nकच्चिन्न निहतः सूत पुत्रो दुःशासनो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, I hope my son Duhshasana, fleeing wretchedly, dejected and spirit broken, has not been killed."}},{"n":47,"text":"कच्चिन्न नीचाचरितं कृतवांस्तात संयुगे ।\nकच्चिन्न निहतः शूरो यथा न क्षत्रिया हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I hope, friend, he did nothing base in battle; I hope the hero was not killed in such a way that kshatriyas are not killed."}},{"n":48,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य वचनं मा युद्धमिति सर्वदा ।\nदुर्योधनो नाभ्यगृह्णान्मूढः पथ्यमिवौषधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, foolish, did not accept Yudhishthira's words, 'No war,' ever, as a sick man will not take wholesome medicine."}},{"n":49,"text":"शरतल्पे शयानेन भीष्मेण सुमहात्मना ।\nपानीयं याचितः पार्थः सोऽविध्यन्मेदिनीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When great-souled Bhishma lay on his bed of arrows and asked for water, Partha pierced the ground."}},{"n":50,"text":"जलस्य धारां विहितां दृष्ट्वा तां पाण्डवेन ह ।\nअब्रवीत्स महाबाहुस्तात संशाम्य पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the stream of water that the Pandava had produced, that strong-armed one said, 'My dear, make peace with the Pandavas."}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रशमाद्धि भवेच्छान्तिर्मदन्तं युद्धमस्तु च ।\nभ्रातृभावेन पृथिवीं भुङ्क्ष्व पाण्डुसुतैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through settling, there may be peace; let the war end with me. Enjoy the earth with the sons of Pandu as brothers.'"}},{"n":52,"text":"अकुर्वन्वचनं तस्य नूनं शोचति मे सुतः ।\nतदिदं समनुप्राप्तं वचनं दीर्घदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son, not following his words, now surely grieves. That word of the far-sighted one has now come true."}},{"n":53,"text":"अहं तु निहतामात्यो हतपुत्रश्च संजय ।\nद्यूततः कृच्छ्रमापन्नो लूनपक्ष इव द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I, Sanjaya, have lost my ministers and my sons; through the dice I have fallen into hardship, like a bird with clipped wings."}},{"n":54,"text":"यथा हि शकुनिं गृह्य छित्त्वा पक्षौ च संजय ।\nविसर्जयन्ति संहृष्टाः क्रीडमानाः कुमारकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As boys play, seizing a bird, cutting its wings and letting it go gleefully, Sanjaya,"}},{"n":55,"text":"छिन्नपक्षतया तस्य गमनं नोपपद्यते ।\nतथाहमपि संप्राप्तो लूनपक्ष इव द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and it cannot fly because its wings are cut, so I too have come to be like a bird with clipped wings."}},{"n":56,"text":"क्षीणः सर्वार्थहीनश्च निर्बन्धुर्ज्ञातिवर्जितः ।\nकां दिशं प्रतिपत्स्यामि दीनः शत्रुवशं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spent, bereft of every aim, without kin, cut off from relatives, which way shall I turn, wretched, fallen into the hands of enemies?"}},{"n":57,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य वृद्ध्यर्थं पृथिवीं योऽजयत्प्रभुः ।\nस जितः पाण्डवैः शूरैः समर्थैर्वीर्यशालिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who conquered the earth for Duryodhana's increase has himself been conquered by the heroic, capable and valiant Pandavas."}},{"n":58,"text":"तस्मिन्हते महेष्वासे कर्णे युधि किरीटिना ।\nके वीराः पर्यवर्तन्त तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that great archer Karna was killed in battle by Kiritin, which heroes turned back? Tell me, Sanjaya."}},{"n":59,"text":"कच्चिन्नैकः परित्यक्तः पाण्डवैर्निहतो रणे ।\nउक्तं त्वया पुरा वीर यथा वीरा निपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I hope no single man was abandoned and killed in battle by the Pandavas. You told me before, hero, how the heroes were felled."}},{"n":60,"text":"भीष्ममप्रतियुध्यन्तं शिखण्डी सायकोत्तमैः ।\nपातयामास समरे सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin brought down Bhishma, best of all weapon-bearers, as he did not fight back, with the best of arrows in the battle."}},{"n":61,"text":"तथा द्रौपदिना द्रोणो न्यस्तसर्वायुधो युधि ।\nयुक्तयोगो महेष्वासः शरैर्बहुभिराचितः ।\nनिहतः खड्गमुद्यम्य धृष्टद्युम्नेन संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Drona, with all weapons laid down, absorbed in yoga, a great archer, covered with many arrows, was killed by Draupada's son Dhrishtadyumna raising his sword, Sanjaya."}},{"n":62,"text":"अन्तरेण हतावेतौ छलेन च विशेषतः ।\nअश्रौषमहमेतद्वै भीष्मद्रोणौ निपातितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two were killed by an intervening deceit above all; I heard that Bhishma and Drona were struck down in this way."}},{"n":63,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणौ हि समरे न हन्याद्वज्रभृत्स्वयम् ।\nन्यायेन युध्यमानौ हि तद्वै सत्यं ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Bhishma and Drona fighting fairly in battle even the thunderbolt-wielder himself could not have killed; I tell you this truly."}},{"n":64,"text":"कर्णं त्वस्यन्तमस्त्राणि दिव्यानि च बहूनि च ।\nकथमिन्द्रोपमं वीरं मृत्युर्युद्धे समस्पृशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Karna, who loosed many divine weapons, equal to Indra, how did death touch that hero in the battle?"}},{"n":65,"text":"यस्य विद्युत्प्रभां शक्तिं दिव्यां कनकभूषणाम् ।\nप्रायच्छद्द्विषतां हन्त्रीं कुण्डलाभ्यां पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He to whom Indra, for his earrings, gave the divine spear gleaming like lightning, adorned with gold, the slayer of enemies,"}},{"n":66,"text":"यस्य सर्पमुखो दिव्यः शरः कनकभूषणः ।\nअशेत निहतः पत्री चन्दनेष्वरिसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"whose divine, golden, snake-mouthed arrow, the slayer of foes, lay struck down amid sandalwood,"}},{"n":67,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणमुखान्वीरान्योऽवमन्य महारथान् ।\nजामदग्न्यान्महाघोरं ब्राह्ममस्त्रमशिक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"he who despised the heroic great chariot-fighters headed by Bhishma and Drona, and learned from Jamadagni's son the terrible Brahma weapon,"}},{"n":68,"text":"यश्च द्रोणमुखान्दृष्ट्वा विमुखानर्दिताञ्शरैः ।\nसौभद्रस्य महाबाहुर्व्यधमत्कार्मुकं शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who, seeing those headed by Drona turned back and afflicted by arrows, shattered with his arrows the bow of the strong-armed son of Subhadra,"}},{"n":69,"text":"यश्च नागायुतप्राणं वातरंहसमच्युतम् ।\nविरथं भ्रातरं कृत्वा भीमसेनमुपाहसत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who made his brother Bhimasena, with the strength of ten thousand elephants and the speed of wind, unfailing, chariotless, and laughed at him,"}},{"n":70,"text":"सहदेवं च निर्जित्य शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nकृपया विरथं कृत्वा नाहनद्धर्मवित्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who defeated Sahadeva with straight-jointed arrows, made him chariotless, and out of compassion, knowing dharma, did not kill him,"}},{"n":71,"text":"यश्च मायासहस्राणि ध्वंसयित्वा रणोत्कटम् ।\nघटोत्कचं राक्षसेन्द्रं शक्रशक्त्याभिजघ्निवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who destroyed thousands of illusions and struck Ghatotkacha, lord of rakshasas, wild in battle, with Shakra's spear,"}},{"n":72,"text":"एतानि दिवसान्यस्य युद्धे भीतो धनंजयः ।\nनागमद्द्वैरथं वीरः स कथं निहतो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"for all these days Dhananjaya, fearing him, did not come to single combat; how was that hero killed in battle?"}},{"n":73,"text":"रथसङ्गो न चेत्तस्य धनुर्वा न व्यशीर्यत ।\nन चेदस्त्राणि निर्णेशुः स कथं निहतः परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If his chariot had not been caught, or his bow had not shattered, or his weapons had not vanished, how could he have been killed by his foes?"}},{"n":74,"text":"को हि शक्तो रणे कर्णं विधुन्वानं महद्धनुः ।\nविमुञ्चन्तं शरान्घोरान्दिव्यान्यस्त्राणि चाहवे ।\nजेतुं पुरुषशार्दूलं शार्दूलमिव वेगितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who in battle can overcome Karna, shaking his great bow, loosing terrible arrows and divine weapons, a tiger among men, swift as a tiger?"}},{"n":75,"text":"ध्रुवं तस्य धनुश्छिन्नं रथो वापि गतो महीम् ।\nअस्त्राणि वा प्रनष्टानि यथा शंससि मे हतम् ।\nन ह्यन्यदनुपश्यामि कारणं तस्य नाशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely his bow was cut, or his chariot sank into the earth, or his weapons were lost, as you tell me he was killed. I see no other cause for his destruction."}},{"n":76,"text":"न हन्यामर्जुनं यावत्तावत्पादौ न धावये ।\nइति यस्य महाघोरं व्रतमासीन्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Until I kill Arjuna, I will not wash my feet.' Such was the terrible vow of that great soul,"}},{"n":77,"text":"यस्य भीतो वने नित्यं धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nत्रयोदश समा निद्रां न लेभे पुरुषर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"from fear of whom King Yudhishthira, lord of dharma, in the forest never found sleep for thirteen years, that bull among men,"}},{"n":78,"text":"यस्य वीर्यवतो वीर्यं समाश्रित्य महात्मनः ।\nमम पुत्रः सभां भार्यां पाण्डूनां नीतवान्बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"relying on whose strength, that valiant and great soul, my son brought the Pandavas' wife into the assembly hall by force,"}},{"n":79,"text":"तत्र चापि सभामध्ये पाण्डवानां च पश्यताम् ।\nदासभार्येति पाञ्चालीमब्रवीत्कुरुसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"and there too in the middle of the hall, while the Pandavas looked on, he called the Panchala princess a slave's wife in the Kuru assembly,"}},{"n":80,"text":"यश्च गाण्डीवमुक्तानां स्पर्शमुग्रमचिन्तयन् ।\nअपतिर्ह्यसि कृष्णेति ब्रुवन्पार्थानवैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who, thinking nothing of the fierce touch of arrows loosed from Gandiva, looked at the Parthas and said, 'Krishna, you have no husband',"}},{"n":81,"text":"यस्य नासीद्भयं पार्थैः सपुत्रैः सजनार्दनैः ।\nस्वबाहुबलमाश्रित्य मुहूर्तमपि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"who for a moment, Sanjaya, had no fear of the Parthas with their sons and Janardana, relying on the strength of his own arms,"}},{"n":82,"text":"तस्य नाहं वधं मन्ये देवैरपि सवासवैः ।\nप्रतीपमुपधावद्भिः किं पुनस्तात पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not think his killing possible even by the gods with Vasava, if they ran against him, much less, my dear, by the Pandavas."}},{"n":83,"text":"न हि ज्यां स्पृशमानस्य तलत्रे चापि गृह्णतः ।\nपुमानाधिरथेः कश्चित्प्रमुखे स्थातुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For when he touches the bowstring and takes hold of the arm-guard, no man can stand before the son of Adhiratha."}},{"n":84,"text":"अपि स्यान्मेदिनी हीना सोमसूर्यप्रभांशुभिः ।\nन वधः पुरुषेन्द्रस्य समरेष्वपलायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth might lose the rays of the moon and sun, but there would be no killing of that lord of men, who never fled in battle."}},{"n":85,"text":"यदि मन्दः सहायेन भ्रात्रा दुःशासनेन च ।\nवासुदेवस्य दुर्बुद्धिः प्रत्याख्यानमरोचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the fool, with his helper his brother Duhshasana, evil-minded, was pleased to reject Vasudeva's proposal,"}},{"n":86,"text":"स नूनमृषभस्कन्धं दृष्ट्वा कर्णं निपातितम् ।\nदुःशासनं च निहतं मन्ये शोचति पुत्रकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"then surely, seeing Karna with his bull's shoulders felled and Duhshasana killed, my son grieves, I think."}},{"n":87,"text":"हतं वैकर्तनं श्रुत्वा द्वैरथे सव्यसाचिना ।\nजयतः पाण्डवान्दृष्ट्वा किं स्विद्दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Vaikartana killed in single combat by Savyasachin and seeing the Pandavas winning, what did Duryodhana say?"}},{"n":88,"text":"दुर्मर्षणं हतं श्रुत्वा वृषसेनं च संयुगे ।\nप्रभग्नं च बलं दृष्ट्वा वध्यमानं महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Durmarshana and Vrishasena were killed in battle, and seeing the army broken and being slaughtered by great chariot-fighters,"}},{"n":89,"text":"पराङ्मुखांस्तथा राज्ञः पलायनपरायणान् ।\nविद्रुतान्रथिनो दृष्ट्वा मन्ये शोचति पुत्रकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the kings turned away, bent on flight, and the charioteers scattered, my son grieves, I think."}},{"n":90,"text":"अनेयश्चाभिमानेन बालबुद्धिरमर्षणः ।\nहतोत्साहं बलं दृष्ट्वा किं स्विद्दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unwise and led by pride, childish-minded, impatient, seeing his army lose heart, what did Duryodhana say?"}},{"n":91,"text":"भ्रातरं निहतं दृष्ट्वा भीमसेनेन संयुगे ।\nरुधिरं पीयमानेन किं स्विद्दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his brother killed in battle by Bhimasena, who drank his blood, what did Duryodhana say?"}},{"n":92,"text":"सह गान्धारराजेन सभायां यदभाषत ।\nकर्णोऽर्जुनं रणे हन्ता हते तस्मिन्किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What did he say when Karna, who in the assembly with the king of Gandhara had said he would kill Arjuna in battle, was killed?"}},{"n":93,"text":"द्यूतं कृत्वा पुरा हृष्टो वञ्चयित्वा च पाण्डवान् ।\nशकुनिः सौबलस्तात हते कर्णे किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, son of Subala, who earlier gleefully played the dice and cheated the Pandavas, what did he say, my dear, when Karna was killed?"}},{"n":94,"text":"कृतवर्मा महेष्वासः सात्वतानां महारथः ।\nकर्णं विनिहतं दृष्ट्वा हार्दिक्यः किमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer Kritavarman, great chariot-fighter of the Satvatas, Hridika's son, what did he say on seeing Karna slain?"}},{"n":95,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः क्षत्रिया वैश्या यस्य शिक्षामुपासते ।\nधनुर्वेदं चिकीर्षन्तो द्रोणपुत्रस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He at whose school brahmanas, kshatriyas and vaishyas wait, wishing to learn archery from the wise son of Drona,"}},{"n":96,"text":"युवा रूपेण संपन्नो दर्शनीयो महायशाः ।\nअश्वत्थामा हते कर्णे किमभाषत संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"young, handsome, good to look on, of great fame, Ashvatthama, what did he say when Karna was killed, Sanjaya?"}},{"n":97,"text":"आचार्यत्वं धनुर्वेदे गतः परमतत्त्ववित् ।\nकृपः शारद्वतस्तात हते कर्णे किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, Sharadvat's son, who has reached mastery as a teacher of archery and knows its highest truth, what did he say, my dear, when Karna was killed?"}},{"n":98,"text":"मद्रराजो महेष्वासः शल्यः समितिशोभनः ।\nदिष्टं तेन हि तत्सर्वं यथा कर्णो निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Madra, Shalya, great archer, ornament of assemblies, how was it fated by him that Karna was killed?"}},{"n":99,"text":"ये च केचन राजानः पृथिव्यां योद्धुमागताः ।\nवैकर्तनं हतं दृष्ट्वा किमभाषन्त संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever kings had come to fight on earth, what did they say, Sanjaya, seeing Vaikartana killed?"}},{"n":100,"text":"कर्णे तु निहते वीरे रथव्याघ्रे नरर्षभे ।\nकिं वो मुखमनीकानामासीत्संजय भागशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the hero Karna, tiger among chariot-fighters, bull among men, was killed, what did the faces of your divisions look like, Sanjaya, one by one?"}},{"n":101,"text":"मद्रराजः कथं शल्यो नियुक्तो रथिनां वरः ।\nवैकर्तनस्य सारथ्ये तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"How was Shalya, king of Madra, best of chariot-fighters, appointed to be charioteer for Vaikartana? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"n":102,"text":"केऽरक्षन्दक्षिणं चक्रं सूतपुत्रस्य संयुगे ।\nवामं चक्रं ररक्षुर्वा के वा वीरस्य पृष्ठतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who guarded the right wheel of the charioteer's son in battle? Who guarded the left wheel, or who was behind the hero?"}},{"n":103,"text":"के कर्णं वाजहुः शूराः के क्षुद्राः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ।\nकथं च वः समेतानां हतः कर्णो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Which heroes followed Karna, which cowards fled in fear? And how was the great chariot-fighter Karna killed while you were all together?"}},{"n":104,"text":"पाण्डवाश्च कथं शूराः प्रत्युदीयुर्महारथम् ।\nसृजन्तं शरवर्षाणि वारिधारा इवाम्बुदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how did the heroic Pandavas face the great chariot-fighter as he showered arrows like a cloud pouring streams of water?"}},{"n":105,"text":"स च सर्पमुखो दिव्यो महेषुप्रवरस्तदा ।\nव्यर्थः कथं समभवत्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how did that divine, snake-mouthed, great and best arrow become useless then? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"n":106,"text":"मामकस्यास्य सैन्यस्य हृतोत्सेधस्य संजय ।\nअवशेषं न पश्यामि ककुदे मृदिते सति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no remnant of this army of mine, its pride gone, Sanjaya, now that its hump has been crushed."}},{"n":107,"text":"तौ हि वीरौ महेष्वासौ मदर्थे कुरुसत्तमौ ।\nभीष्मद्रोणौ हतौ श्रुत्वा को न्वर्थो जीवितेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that those two heroic, great archers, best of Kurus, Bhishma and Drona, were killed for my sake, what use is life to me?"}},{"n":108,"text":"न मृष्यामि च राधेयं हतमाहवशोभिनम् ।\nयस्य बाह्वोर्बलं तुल्यं कुञ्जराणां शतं शतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot bear that Radheya, glory of the battlefield, is dead, the strength of whose arms equalled hundreds and hundreds of elephants."}},{"n":109,"text":"द्रोणे हते च यद्वृत्तं कौरवाणां परैः सह ।\nसंग्रामे नरवीराणां तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And tell me, Sanjaya, what happened between the Kauravas and the enemy, between the human heroes in the battle, after Drona was killed."}},{"n":110,"text":"यथा च कर्णः कौन्तेयैः सह युद्धमयोजयत् ।\nयथा च द्विषतां हन्ता रणे शान्तस्तदुच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell how Karna joined battle with the sons of Kunti, and how that slayer of foes was stilled in the fight.\""}}]}]}